SUBQUERY = I need the result of one query to solve another query
1. What is the requirement?
2. What information do we need first?
3. Does that information come from another query?
4. Will the inner query return one value or multiple values?
5. Does the inner query depend on the outer row?
6. Which operator/pattern fits?
7. Now write the SQL.
8. Explain your query in English

One value        → Scalar subquery
Multiple values  → IN / ANY / ALL
Existence        → EXISTS
Non-existence    → NOT EXISTS
Outer-row dependent → Correlated subquery
Temporary result set → Derived table

If you memorize 20 subquery queries today, you will forget them next month. If you understand what information the outer query needs from the inner query, you can construct the query even when the interviewer gives you a completely new problem

